.TH WAYHUD 1 "2026-09-01" "wayhud" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayhud \- heads\-up text overlay for sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayhud
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fITEXT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayhud
puts a message on screen above every window, as a Wayland layer\-shell
overlay on the
.B overlay
layer. The text can appear all at once or be typed out terminal\-style with
a caret and a synthesised blip per keystroke, and it leaves with one of
several exit animations.
.PP
It is a one\-shot program: it shows the message, waits, and exits. Two
concurrent invocations are two processes and two layer surfaces, which the
compositor stacks.
.PP
The overlay keeps an empty input region, so it never intercepts pointer or
keyboard events \- whatever is underneath stays usable.
.PP
.I TEXT
is taken from the command line; if it is omitted or given as
.BR - ,
the message is read from standard input instead. In a command\-line
argument the escapes
.BR \en ,
.B \et
and
.B \e\e
are expanded, because sway runs
.B exec
through
.BR sh ,
which has no
.BR $'...'
quoting. Text arriving on standard input is used verbatim.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fISPEC\fR"
Which outputs to show on:
.B current
(the output sway currently has focus on),
.B all
(every enabled output), or a comma\-separated list of connector names such as
.BR DP\-3,eDP\-1 .
Default:
.BR current .
.IP
.B current
queries sway over its IPC socket, because Wayland gives a client no way to
learn which output is focused. Without
.B SWAYSOCK
it fails rather than guessing. A named output that does not exist is
reported and skipped; if nothing matches at all, that is an error.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR"
How long the fully revealed text stays up. Measured from the
.I end
of the reveal, not from start\-up, so a slow typewriter does not eat into
the reading time. Default: 5.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-style " \fINAME\fR"
Style preset from the config file. Default:
.BR default .
An unknown name is an error.
.TP
.BR \-\-font " \fIDESC\fR"
Pango font description, e.g.
.BR "\(dqLythMono Nerd Font 72\(dq" .
Note that the family name must match fontconfig exactly; a family that does
not resolve falls back silently to the default font.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " \fICOLOUR\fR"
Fill colour of the glyphs. Any colour GTK's CSS parser accepts:
.BR #b8bb26 ,
.BR "rgba(184,187,38,0.8)" ,
.BR green .
.TP
.BR \-\-outline " \fICOLOUR\fR"
Outline colour, or
.B none
to draw the glyphs flat. The outline is a real cairo stroke around the glyph
path, not a shadow, so it stays clean at display sizes.
.IP
Its width comes from
.B outline_width
in the config. Left unset there, it scales with the font size, keeping the
halo a fixed fraction of the stem: a constant width that looks like a fine
contour at 72pt reads as fake bold at 24pt.
.TP
.BR \-\-position " \fIPLACE\fR"
Where the text block sits:
.BR center ,
.BR top ,
.BR bottom ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
or a hyphenated pair such as
.B top\-left
or
.BR bottom\-right ,
in either order. A centred axis ignores the configured margin.
.TP
.BR \-\-typewriter " \fICPS\fR"
Reveal speed in characters per second.
.B 0
reveals the whole message instantly.
.TP
.BR \-\-vanish " \fIKIND\fR[:\fIMS\fR]"
Exit animation, one of:
.RS
.TP
.B instant
Gone on the frame the hold expires.
.TP
.B fade
Alpha to zero.
.TP
.B collapse
CRT power\-off: squashes to a bright line, blooms wider, blinks out.
.TP
.B wash\-down
A soft edge sweeps top to bottom, erasing as it passes.
.TP
.B wash\-up
The same, bottom to top.
.TP
.B untype
The caret walks back and eats the text, blipping as it goes. The only exit
that makes a sound.
.TP
.B dissolve
The glyphs fall apart into blocks in a fixed pseudo\-random order.
.RE
.IP
Without
.RI : MS
the flag keeps whatever duration the preset already had, so effects can be
cycled without restating the timing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sound
Stay silent regardless of what the style asks for.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Take
.I TEXT
literally: do not expand
.BR \en ,
.B \et
or
.BR \e\e .
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Config file to read. Default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wayhud/config.toml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B wayhud
reads
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wayhud/config.toml
(falling back to
.IR ~/.config/wayhud/config.toml ).
A missing file is fine; a malformed one is an error, as is an unknown key,
so a typo is reported instead of being silently ignored.
.PP
The file is a flat map of named presets. Presets do
.I not
inherit from one another: every field left unset falls back to the built\-in
default, never to
.BR [style.default] .
.PP
.RS
.nf
[style.default]
font = "LythMono Nerd Font 72"
color = "#b8bb26"
outline = "#1d2021"
# outline_width = 5.0    # omit: scales with the font size
halign = "center"        # start | center | end
valign = "center"
margin = 64
line_align = "left"      # left | center | right
timeout_ms = 5000
reveal = { kind = "typewriter", cps = 28, cursor = true }
vanish = { kind = "collapse", ms = 420 }
sound = { enabled = true, freq = 2100.0, decay_ms = 38.0, gain = 0.22, every = 1 }
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B reveal
is either
.B { kind = "instant" }
or
.BR "{ kind = \(dqtypewriter\(dq, cps = N, cursor = BOOL }" .
.B vanish
takes the same kinds as
.BR \-\-vanish ,
with
.B wash
carrying an extra
.B dir
of
.B down
or
.BR up .
.SH SOUND
The typewriter blip is synthesised at run time rather than loaded from a
file, so the program carries no assets. The knobs match those of
.BR blyamk (1);
a sound dialled in there with
.B blyamk \-v
transfers verbatim into a
.B [style.X.sound]
block.
.PP
The entire click track is mixed before the first frame and written to
PulseAudio in one go, so the clicks stay locked to the characters instead of
inheriting the sound server's per\-write scheduling jitter. If no sound
server is reachable, the message is still shown and the failure is reported
on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
A message on the focused output, default style:
.B wayhud \(dqSYSTEM ONLINE\(dq
.TP
Ten seconds, every screen, pinned to the top:
.B wayhud \-o all \-t 10 \-\-position top \(dqBUILD FAILED\(dq
.TP
Two lines from a keybinding in the sway config:
.B bindsym $mod+Shift+h exec wayhud \(dqLOCKED\enBACK IN 5\(dq
.TP
Piped in, no animation, no sound:
.B echo \(dq$(uptime)\(dq | wayhud \-\-typewriter 0 \-\-no\-sound
.TP
Self\-destructing note:
.B wayhud \-s spy \-\-vanish untype:900 \(dqTHIS MESSAGE WILL SELF DESTRUCT\(dq
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWAYSOCK
Path to sway's IPC socket. Required for
.BR "\-\-output current" .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the config file. Falls back to
.IR $HOME/.config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The message was shown and its lifetime ran out.
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments, unreadable or invalid config, no matching output, or no
display.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR swaymsg (1),
.BR pango-markup (7)
